# Phase 1a Drive Ledger

Phase 1a makes re-drive state explicit in the capsule supervisor Durable Object instead of inferring completion from best-effort artifact reads.

## Decision

The per-run drive ledger is the authority for completed run phases:

- `plan-pinned`
- `execution-completed`
- `verification-completed`
- `capture-completed`

Each phase entry records the artifact ref, artifact hash, media type, receipt kind, completion time, drive generation, and the artifact commit sha that proves the phase. `WorkflowApp.run()` only skips a phase when the ledger says that phase completed, then reconstructs from the artifact at the recorded commit sha. Ledger-silent phases run normally.

Drive generations fence writes. The supervisor admits a new generation for each drive, persists it in the ledger, and passes it into `WorkflowApp.run()`. Status projection writes and phase ledger writes assert the generation before mutating state. A stale generation receives a typed `stale_drive_generation` rejection and aborts quietly instead of writing blockers or ledger entries.

## Receipts

- Spec source: `.brain/resources/phase1a-drive-ledger-spec.md`.
- Code surfaces: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-capsule-supervisor.ts`, `src/app/application/workflow-app.ts`, `src/app/application/ports.ts`, `src/app/domain/schemas.ts`, `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-artifacts-store.ts`, `src/app/infrastructure/memory-adapters.ts`.
- Integration tests:
  - `tests/integration/cloudflare-run-async-driver.test.ts` proves stale generation rejection and ledger persistence across supervisor instance swaps.
  - `tests/integration/workflow-app.test.ts` proves ledger-driven re-drive skips the planner and dynamic execution phases, then resumes at verification/capture.

## Verification

Passed:

```bash
pnpm check
pnpm typecheck
pnpm verify
pnpm exec vitest run tests/integration/cloudflare-run-async-driver.test.ts tests/integration/workflow-app.test.ts
```

Additional full-suite probe:

```bash
pnpm exec vitest run
```

The Codex sandbox showed environmental failures (local relay HTTP tests cannot bind `127.0.0.1`, and fresh worktrees lack the generated `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json` for `prototypes/workflow-monitor-ui` until `svelte-kit sync` runs). Outside the sandbox, with `svelte-kit sync` applied, the full suite is green: 342/342. Note `pnpm verify` is only `pnpm check && pnpm typecheck`; it does not run tests.
